<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pandacan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pandacan is a district of the City of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, on the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasig-river">Pasig River</a>. Originally a riverside settlement within the lands of the pre-colonial polity of Namayan, it developed as a separate town under Spanish rule and was incorporated into Manila in 1901. In the 20th century it became known for its large oil depots.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pandacan.jpg" alt="Pandacan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patrickroque01 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pandacan_skyline_(Manila;_12-02-2023).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
